## Findings

Executed new (not inherited) analysis of complete native matrices: GSE115930, 24 labelled libraries across E21/P6/P18 (four WT and four transgenic per age), fractional RSEM expected counts preserved; GSE252209, five labelled libraries at 5 weeks (two Acly f/f control and three Acly f/f;Mpz-Cre). AW/AK identities were verified against author DE-table group means and exact raw columns for all 27,096 author DE rows. Whole matrices and all gene-contrast rows are retained. Median-of-ratios within each age, log2(normalized+.5), CPM sensitivity, sample-level conditional Welch intervals/exact unpaired permutations and leave-library/gene sensitivities were executed. See inputs/analysis-plan.json for the pre-computation rules. RNA, mapping/summary and validation receipts exited 0; Ruff passed.

Strongest discrimination: at P18, Pmp22-transgenic nerves have a sterol-synthesis score ~0.83 log2 lower relative to myelin7; independent Acly-loss nerves have the opposite relative score (~+0.80 log2) while their Pmp22 RNA falls (~-0.75 log2). Myelin/Pmp22 RNA loss is not a universal readout of suppressed sterol transcription, and neither is a measurement of sterol flux. Signs persist under CPM and prespecified leave-library/gene checks. Source authors already described developmental lipid dysregulation (Fledrich) and maintained SREBP-target expression with downregulated myelin genes after Acly loss (Schneider et al., doi:10.1002/glia.24620; attribution corrected after checking primary front matter, not Zhao); the general mechanism is not newly discovered here.

Post-discovery candidate, corrected component transcription: the three-gene export module conceals relative transporter differences. At P18, Abca1 +1.757706 [1.476337,2.039075] versus Abcg1 -0.263582 [-0.562113,0.034949] log2; after Acly loss, Abca1 +1.040270 [-0.645128,2.725668] versus Abcg1 -1.702455 [-2.415823,-0.989087]. Log-ratio shifts were always correct: +2.021 (conditional CI 1.546..2.497) and +2.743 (1.477..4.008). P18 Abcg1 repression is not independently established; Acly Abca1 has a wide conditional interval. The supported point association is increased ABCA1-relative-to-ABCG1 RNA, not separately replicated repression/induction. Acly permutation p=0.1 is the ten-assignment resolution limit. These are RNA contrasts, not enhanced efflux; state/composition remain live alternatives.

